## KNOWN OPEN ISSUES

### 1. Quiz layout shift (jitter) — WORKAROUND APPLIED, NOT FULLY SOLVED
User reported the page "shaking up and down a little, constantly" — after
investigation (see DECISIONS LOG for the false start), root cause was:
different quiz questions/the result card have different natural content
heights, so switching between them via React state causes a real layout
reflow, nudging content below the quiz widget up/down. This is NOT an
animation loop — it happens once per click, then stops, which is why it
was initially hard to diagnose (first theory — SocialFollowCTA's icon
resize interval — was WRONG, user correctly pushed back on it).

**Current fix**: hardcoded `minHeight: '420px'` on both the question-view
and result-view wrapper divs in `QuizWidget.tsx`. This works for the
CURRENT test post's quiz (2 questions, short labels, short result
descriptions) but is a magic number — a future quiz with more questions,
longer option labels, or a longer result description could exceed 420px
and the jitter would return. **User was asked whether to build a more
robust version (auto-measures actual content, no magic number) and had
not yet answered when this handoff was written — this is an explicit
open decision, not a forgotten task.**

