## AUTHOR MATCHING — IMPORTANT, EASY TO GET WRONG AGAIN

`resolveAuthor()` in `src/data/authors.ts` does CASE-INSENSITIVE SUBSTRING
matching, not exact matching:
- Contains `"jyoti"` or `"jyotika"` → Jyotika Verma
- Contains `"ri"` or `"gaurav"` → Gaurav Verma (note: `"ri"` as a bare
  substring is broad — any future author name containing "ri" would
  misattribute to Gaurav)
- Anything else → resolves to nothing, AuthorCard silently doesn't render

Always use the exact strings `"Jyotika Verma"` or `"Gaurav Verma"` in
frontmatter. This is documented in the README but repeating it here since
it already caused one real, silent bug in this build.

