## ORIGINAL RESEARCH (unchanged, carried over from the first handoff)

### Feb 2026 Google Discover Core Update (first-ever Discover-only core update)
- 3 levers: (1) local relevance by country, (2) reduced clickbait/sensationalism,
  (3) more in-depth/original/timely content from sites with topic-level
  expertise (not domain-level).
- Google deployed an ML classifier comparing headline promise vs. actual
  content delivery — headline-engineering-without-substance is actively
  suppressed, not rewarded.
- Content clusters (pillar + spokes) are a structural requirement for
  Discover now, not just an SEO nicety.

### Technical eligibility (hard gates, from Google's own docs)
- Hero image: ≥1200px wide, 16:9 aspect ratio, >300,000 total pixels.
  Nail Feed uses 1200x675 — CORRECT, do not change to /blog's 1200x630.
- `max-image-preview:large` required — CONFIRMED ALREADY PRESENT in
  layout.tsx (see DECISIONS LOG — this corrects the original handoff's
  claim that it was absent).
- Only the hero image needs the size spec — body images are unconstrained.

### Content behavior
- Discover traffic comes in short bursts: ~24-72hrs typical, up to 7-14
  days for content reinforced by a strong topic cluster.
- No official Discover CTR benchmark exists — track via Search Console's
  Discover tab, don't quote invented numbers.
- Lifestyle/beauty is an explicitly named durable Discover category.
- Ranking is NOT keyword-first — matches predicted interest/behavior
  profiles (entities/interest clusters, not keywords — John Shehata/
  NewzDash is the most-cited practitioner source on this).
- Early engagement (click → stay/scroll) creates a feedback loop; bad
  early engagement kills reach fast. **This is the actual justification
  for the widget system built in this handoff** — reaction/poll/quiz
  exist to increase early on-page engagement signal, not as generic
  "fun features."
- Optimizing for Discover does not hurt Search — measured separately in
  GSC, and Discover best practices overlap with SEO best practices anyway.

### Headline guidance
- Negative-angle-plus-solution and "trending now" titles are fine ONLY if
  the post delivers on the promise — Google's classifier actively
  suppresses overpromising, this isn't just a style guideline.
- ~60-65 characters is roughly where Discover truncates titles.

### Word count / image count
- Target: 900-1300 words (not /blog's 2200-3500).
- Body images: 2-5, light — scale toward the higher end for roundups,
  fewer for opinion/Q&A pieces.

### GSC content-gap audit (flagged as a process to formalize, not yet built)
- Standing monthly input: pull GSC queries with impressions where the
  ranking page is only adjacent/related, not a direct match — that gap
  list becomes new Nail Feed topics. **Still not built** — this is
  unrelated to the widget work in this handoff, remains open from the
